
# Browser console implementation. Internal: reached only through the public console API.
#
# There was none, and `console.tree` is what `log` and `error` reach, so nothing that printed a line could be
# built for the browser at all. `term cast`, which builds an SSR app for Cloudflare and borrows this env, failed
# on a FRESHLY SCAFFOLDED project with `the name "write-error" is not defined`, pointing into the stdlib rather
# than at anything the person had written.
#
# `console` is a real global here, in a browser and in a Cloudflare Worker alike, so this docks it directly and
# needs no runtime shim, exactly as the node implementation does.

dock load
  load <global:console>, name console

task write-line
  take message, like text
  like void
  call console/log
    read message

task write-error
  take message, like text
  like void
  call console/error
    read message
